decisions:
  - id: conductor-multi-workspace
    decision: Conductor watches all agents across all projects, not just current workspace
    rationale: Field test showed cross-session messages invisible because thread watcher only scoped to one workspace. Multi-workspace scan at launch + re-scan on view open.
  - id: thread-prefix-removal
    decision: Removed thr-orch- hard filter, replaced with 2-hour staleness cutoff
    rationale: The prefix filter silently dropped all non-orchestration threads. Cross-team discussion threads were invisible in Conductor.
  - id: pan-consensus
    decision: PAN sits ON TOP of agent frameworks, not alongside them. A/B experiment is priority zero.
    rationale: 'Cross-team Symphony debate reached consensus: PAN should not build its own ReAct/tool/network stack. Build a framework bridge instead. Prove knowledge injection works before building infrastructure.'
